      "writtenOn": "2024-09-25T11:56:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s basically what `optional` means. Labels are optional in descriptors and I believe that Austin chose to use `NullableStringView` in `SetLabel` to match what\u0027s in the descriptor, even if handling in Dawn always decays the nil string to `\"\"`. If that\u0027s something that we want to change (either making these not `optional`, or handling the `nil` string to unset the label), I\u0027d like to do it in a follow-up to unblock other CLs.\n\nIt\u0027s also useful in the Kotlin bindings to generate `String?` instead of `String`,",
      "parentUuid": "91a8cd9e_24d7069d",
      "revId": "17cada87d0e00341124329cf79c5523f73342b4d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
