      "lineNbr": 357,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000015
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-25T19:03:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should change it in Dawn eventually, but it definitely doesn\u0027t need to be now. (I just wasn\u0027t sure whether Dawn still internally allowed labels to be null or not.)\n\nIn the Kotlin bindings I wouldn\u0027t expect `SetLabel(null)` to work, e.g. you can\u0027t `.label \u003d null` or `.label \u003d undefined` in JS. (those will set the label to `\"null\"` or `\"undefined\"` due to IDL conversion rules)\n\nI don\u0027t know what the Kotlin looks like for descriptors but they should behave similarly to JS, where omitting a label sets the label to `\"\"`. (In JS `label: undefined` also defaults to `\"\"` but that\u0027s a JS-ism.)\n\nAnyway pretty sure no change is necessary in this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "8ed0ee76_2165a18f",
      "revId": "17cada87d0e00341124329cf79c5523f73342b4d",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
